      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can help you craft a rejection email that's both professional and polite. You can use the following template as a starting point:\n\n\"Dear [Candidate Name],\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the status of your application for the Senior Engineering position at [Company Name]. We appreciate the time and effort you took to interview with us, and we were impressed by your skills and experience.\n\nAfter careful consideration, we have decided to move forward with another candidate whose skills and fit for the role align more closely with our current needs. Please know that this decision is in no way a reflection on your abilities or potential as an engineer.\n\nWe appreciate your interest in joining our team and wish you the best of luck in your ongoing job search. If you have any questions or concerns, please don't hesitate to reach out.\n\nSincerely,\n[Your Name]\"\n\nYou can customize this template to fit your company's tone and style, but the key is to be sincere, professional, and respectful.",
      "source": "target",
